MID_EV14_107_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_107_m01_001: A moment, Miss Leda?
MID_EV14_107_m01_002: Since we last spoke of Father Mahdel, I have\ncontinued looking into him.
MID_EV14_107_m01_003: And...I learned something. He has ties to the Order\nof Mithras.
MID_EV14_107_m01_004: <NCA>Ask for details.
MID_EV14_107_m01_005: <ACA>What is that? I'm not familiar.
MID_EV14_107_m01_006: I'd call it a branch of the temple of Dagda, but...\nthat's not quite right.
MID_EV14_107_m01_007: Frankly, even we don't have all the facts figured out.
MID_EV14_107_m01_008: I know you have your flaws, but you're a vulkan\nfrom Kalla's temple. You don't have it figured out?
MID_EV14_107_m01_009: I know it's painful to hear, but they are an\nenigmatic group, even among the temples.
MID_EV14_107_m01_010: And their history is long. They were founded by\nDagda, like the temples.
MID_EV14_107_m01_011: They specialize in alchemy and are believed to have\ncontributed greatly to the development of the empire.
MID_EV14_107_m01_012: How did Father Mahdel get tied up with them?
MID_EV14_107_m01_013: By all accounts, the man confined himself at home\nafter the Sun Corridor Scandal and his downfall.
MID_EV14_107_m01_014: He devoted his time to studying ways of extending\nthe human lifespan.
MID_EV14_107_m01_015: It was probably around then that he came into\ncontact with the Order.
MID_EV14_107_m01_016: Not long after, Father Mahdel was sent to work in\nOrtill county.
MID_EV14_107_m01_017: So, you're unable to look into the Order of Mithras?
MID_EV14_107_m01_018: Investigating the Order is not without its difficulties.\nOr its risks.
MID_EV14_107_m01_019: Many who run afoul of the Order go missing.\nYou should do your best not to get close.
MID_EV14_107_m01_020: What I want to know is why the Order has been left\nto their own devices for so long.
MID_EV14_107_m01_021: Here's one theory—far-fetched as it may sound.
MID_EV14_107_m01_022: Could it be possible there's a conspiracy here that is\ngreater than we imagined?
MID_EV14_107_m01_023: The Coris Mine, the Cydonia Massacre, the Order of\nMithras's dealings. The Mahdel List.
MID_EV14_107_m01_024: King Hasdrubal's assassination in Arago.
MID_EV14_107_m01_025: What if all these things are connected somehow?
MID_EV14_107_m01_026: And if so, who's spinning this web of evil? What are\ntheir plans and motivations?
MID_EV14_107_m01_027: Slow down there. That seems too convenient,\nthinking it's all connected.
MID_EV14_107_m01_028: You may be right. The more I try to investigate these\nmatters, the less I understand.
MID_EV14_107_m01_029: Well, we're past the point of turning back.
MID_EV14_107_m01_030: So we are. The enemy's not going to ignore us after\nwe stole the ghost carriage.
MID_EV14_107_m01_031: I fear we may have released forces much bigger\nthan us. Caution, Miss Leda.
MID_EV14_039_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_039_m01_001: Hello! Anna here for your routine administrative\nannouncement about the Heroic Games.
MID_EV14_039_m01_002: Rose Tempest, the details of your next match have\nbeen finalized.
MID_EV14_039_m01_003: Since when was this routine?
MID_EV14_039_m01_004: Let's not get hung up on that, OK?
MID_EV14_039_m01_005: Everything's written in this brief here, so be sure to\ngive it a read.
MID_EV14_039_m01_006: <TLP>Rose Tempest\n\nMatch: Third Qualifier of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Bragança Brotherhood\nLeader: Inyoni\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}
MID_EV14_039_m01_007: As you probably know, it's been three months since\nthe games started.
MID_EV14_039_m01_008: In that time, a lot of the clans have dropped out.
MID_EV14_039_m01_009: Those who managed to stay in are all considerably\npowerful players.
MID_EV14_039_m01_010: Present company included, of course!
MID_EV14_039_m01_011: Yes, it's as you say. If the weakest have been culled,\nwe'll need to be more cautious.
MID_EV14_039_m01_012: Exactly what I was getting at. Heehee. Same as ever.\nNothing gets by the Demon Bear of Baphos!
MID_EV14_039_m01_013: Uh, Buccar, do you and Anna know each other?
MID_EV14_039_m01_014: I would call us acquaintances.
MID_EV14_039_m01_015: There was a time when I held the rank of pilus prior\nin Dagsion.
MID_EV14_039_m01_016: Anna was bustling around Dagsion even then.
MID_EV14_039_m01_017: But I will say I'm surprised she remembered me.
MID_EV14_039_m01_018: Well, you loomed so large! And people had such high\nexpectations of you, so you made an impression.
MID_EV14_039_m01_019: Anyway, I'm looking forward to your next match.\nNo doubt it'll be one to watch!
MID_EV14_039_m01_020: And just like that, she's gone! Busy as ever, I see.
MID_EV14_039_m01_021: I assumed she was on the younger side, but based on\nall that...could she be a demigod?
MID_EV14_039_m01_022: Hey, by the way, Leda! I put out feelers in the city.
MID_EV14_039_m01_023: Didn't hear talk at all about the ghost carriage\ngetting stolen.
MID_EV14_039_m01_024: Hmm. When the shipment failed to arrive, I assumed\nthe repercussions would be quick to come.
MID_EV14_039_m01_025: It's strange we've seen none. That's not to say we can\nrest easy, of course. Our foes are thorough.
MID_EV14_039_m01_026: Maybe I'm missing something, but...isn't it a good\nthing that they're not chasing us down?
MID_EV14_039_m01_027: No. The enemy will take the carriage's loss as a\nmajor blow.
MID_EV14_039_m01_028: Their silence doesn't mean they won't make a move.\nOnly that they haven't made one yet.
MID_EV14_039_m01_029: All we can do now is wait.
MID_EV14_039_m01_030: Hmm. Yes, but...I might take a look around the\ncity myself.
MID_EV14_039_m01_031: Oh! Leaving, are you? Then could I ask a small favor,\nLeilidahna?
MID_EV14_039_m01_032: I've been asked to run an errand for Kalla,\nand I'd like your help, if you don't mind.
MID_EV14_039_m01_033: <NCA>Ask what the errand is.
MID_EV14_039_m01_034: Of course I don't mind, but...it might depend on what\nthe errand is. What did she ask you to do?
MID_EV14_039_m01_035: Procure a few good bottles of that young ghosh that's\nbegun showing up on the market.
MID_EV14_039_m01_036: Why would Kalla want that? Don't the aged\nones taste better?
MID_EV14_039_m01_037: There's merit in tasting the younger brews to get a\nsense of the quality of the year's harvest.
MID_EV14_039_m01_038: But I imagine she also enjoys partaking of seasonal\nflavors for their ephemerality!
MID_EV14_039_m01_039: Alright. I'll look for some while I'm out.
MID_EV14_040_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_040_m01_001: Leda, if I'm not mistaken? A moment?
MID_EV14_040_m01_002: Sorry, I don't believe we've met.
MID_EV14_040_m01_003: My master would like to speak with you about your\nrecent theft.
MID_EV14_040_m01_004: Please, accompany me, won't you?
MID_EV14_040_m01_005: Hmm. You've had eyes on us for some time, I take it.\nHow else would you know who I was?
MID_EV14_040_m01_006: Your performance in the Heroic Games has been\nexceptional.
MID_EV14_040_m01_007: I'd wager it would be more difficult to find someone\nin this city who doesn't recognize you.
MID_EV14_040_m01_008: Alright. Next question—if your master wants to\nspeak with me, why don't they come themself?
MID_EV14_040_m01_009: My master is of a cautious disposition. They rarely\ngo out in public to meet anyone.
MID_EV14_040_m01_010: Let alone dangerous individuals who seize valuable\nassets by force.
MID_EV14_040_m01_011: Guess it's hard to argue with that.
MID_EV14_040_m01_012: You may not believe me, as the person who stole it,\nbut I have no interest in orichalcum.
MID_EV14_040_m01_013: No one would buy it from us in the first place.\nRight now it's just taking up space.
MID_EV14_040_m01_014: That said...I could be amenable to selling it to you,\nif the price was right.
MID_EV14_040_m01_015: My master promises that no ill will befall you.
MID_EV14_040_m01_016: I wonder about that. In any case, I'm not following\nyou anywhere. I know a trap when I see one.
MID_EV14_040_m01_017: Let's see... Say we deliver the ghost carriage tonight\non Evermist Plain. Would that work?
MID_EV14_040_m01_018: I will discuss it with my master.
MID_EV14_040_m01_019: You would be well-advised to stick to your word.
MID_EV14_040_m01_020: *sigh*
MID_EV14_040_m01_021: How extraordinary...
MID_EV14_040_m01_022: Miss Leda, it's dangerous to deal with an\norganization we understand so little.
MID_EV14_040_m01_023: And doing so on your own! What were you thinking?
MID_EV14_040_m01_024: What choice did I have? He singled ME out.
MID_EV14_040_m01_025: Besides, better that we're meeting on Evermist\nPlain than going to negotiate in their base.
MID_EV14_040_m01_026: But...you've given them time—albeit briefly—\nto prepare.
MID_EV14_040_m01_027: It's not out of the question that they've set a trap.
MID_EV14_040_m01_028: If we want to uncover the truth, we'll have to\nconfront the bandaged man anyway.
MID_EV14_040_m01_029: And if he dares to try springing a trap, then fine.\nWe'll handle it.
MID_EV14_040_m01_030: As long as I can finally see his face.
MID_EV14_041_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_041_m01_001: Visibility here is as poor as ever. We'll have no way\nto see enemies coming.
MID_EV14_041_m01_002: Because winds do not flow through this terrain,\nthe mist tends to accumulate.
MID_EV14_041_m01_003: <NCA>Be cautious.
MID_EV14_041_m01_004: <NCB>Be confident.
MID_EV14_041_m01_005: <ACA>Can never be too careful. Mu, keep an eye out.
MID_EV14_041_m01_006: <ACA>OK! Leave it to me!
MID_EV14_041_m01_007: <ACB>It'll be fine. Besides, the mist will make it easier for\nus to escape if we need to.
MID_EV14_041_m01_008: <ACB>Oh, you are as frustratingly passionate as ever,\nmy dear.
MID_EV14_041_m01_009: A pleasure to meet you. I'm Mandalan. I thank you\nfor giving me this chance to negotiate.
MID_EV14_041_m01_010: Mandalan, you say? I've heard the name.
MID_EV14_041_m01_011: You're the merchant who appeared in Dagsion out of\nnowhere and amassed a fast fortune.
MID_EV14_041_m01_012: If the rumors are true, you're also a misanthrope who\nnever goes out in public. This is quite the rarity.
MID_EV14_041_m01_013: Mandalan. Would you remove that bandage so that\nwe can see your face?
MID_EV14_041_m01_014: Apologies...but the bandages are here for your sake.\nI have terrible burns all over my body and face.
MID_EV14_041_m01_015: I would never want to expose anyone else to my\nunsightly appearance.
MID_EV14_041_m01_016: I understand. I'm...sorry I asked. You can keep\nthem on.
MID_EV14_041_m01_017: Well? Have you brought it?
MID_EV14_041_m01_018: Yes, of course.
MID_EV14_041_m01_019: Here we are, Leilidahna! My, it really is a large\ncarriage, isn't it?
MID_EV14_041_m01_020: Oh, I appreciate this. And the cargo is untouched?
MID_EV14_041_m01_021: Your appreciation is premature. Our negotiations\nhave only just started.
MID_EV14_041_m01_022: One million ought to suffice, yes? Now return it.
MID_EV14_041_m01_023: A million! That's more money than I've ever even\nTHOUGHT about. Whew, little woozy...
MID_EV14_041_m01_024: No.
MID_EV14_041_m01_025: Th-three million, then!
MID_EV14_041_m01_026: This is getting us nowhere. What I want from you\nisn't your money.
MID_EV14_041_m01_029: I can tell you nothing. If I did, we would both be\nswiftly killed.
MID_EV14_041_m01_030: Leda, you must accept these terms. You must!
MID_EV14_041_m01_031: Oh, I know—if it would satisfy you, I could arrange\na fight with Bertrand!
MID_EV14_041_m01_032: Oh?!
MID_EV14_041_m01_033: Now that's a little more appealing. But I'm still\ngoing to pass.
MID_EV14_041_m01_034: Why, Leda?!
MID_EV14_041_m01_035: You know...I hate the way you smell. It's this terrible\nrotting stench.
MID_EV14_041_m01_036: Why would I make a deal with a man who reeks\nof evil?
MID_EV14_041_m01_037: I'm going to cut my own path to Bertrand—so, I don't\nneed anything from you.
MID_EV14_041_m01_038: The discussion's over, eh? That's disappointing.
MID_EV14_041_m01_039: You!
MID_EV14_041_m01_040: You'll have to come with us. Don't worry, there's\nno danger—as long as you don't resist.
MID_EV14_041_m01_041: What a shame. You're such a gifted artist, Leda...
MID_EV14_041_m01_042: and such a bad negotiator. You would have had no\nluck as a merchant.
MID_EV14_041_m01_043: Well...it looks like we would have been ambushed\neven if we did accept his terms.
MID_EV14_041_m01_044: Leilidahna, what ever do we do? We are surrounded!
MID_EV14_041_m01_045: I wouldn't have guessed the Twin Jewels of Arago\nwere tied up in this.
MID_EV14_041_m01_046: I think I've heard of them before...
MID_EV14_041_m01_047: The Twin Jewels are the pride of Arago's army.\nDifficult opponents for us.
MID_EV14_041_m01_048: And...they took part in the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_EV14_041_m01_049: Why are we getting sent out to do so many chores?\nThat guy works his people too hard.
MID_EV14_041_m01_050: I agree. It's bad for our reputation. The Twin Errand\nBoys of Arago.
MID_EV14_041_m01_051: I didn't expect to see Arago's regular army stand\nagainst us. What should we do?
MID_EV14_041_m01_052: What choice is there? If they're going to stand in\nour way, we'll have to push them aside.
MID_EV14_041_m01_053: Hey, you all! Want to hear a song?
MID_EV14_067_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_067_m01_001: Now, Sirocco!
MID_EV14_067_m01_002: Leave it to me.
MID_EV14_067_m01_003: No! What are you doing?!
MID_EV14_067_m01_004: No. NO!
MID_EV14_067_m01_005: Soldiers, begin collecting orichalcum now! If even\none trace is not retrieved, I will be killed!
MID_EV14_067_m01_006: Let's get out of here while we have the chance!
MID_EV14_067_m01_007: That woman—she blew up the carriage!
MID_EV14_067_m01_008: Heh. Hehe... Hahaha! Oh, what a pickle. To think\nshe'd pull one over on me!
MID_EV14_067_m01_009: Crafty. Impressive that she outmaneuvered us—\nyou especially.
MID_EV14_067_m01_010: Indeed. That one's not a cornered rat baring\nher fangs. She's a beast of prey on the loose.
MID_EV14_067_m01_011: We should be far enough away now, right?
MID_EV14_067_m01_012: I still can't fathom how those two got tangled up in\nall of this.
MID_EV14_067_m01_013: If they're mobilizing the regular army...we must have\nstepped into something big.
MID_EV14_067_m01_014: <NCA>Mull it over.
MID_EV14_067_m01_015: I'd thought Lechner was perhaps acting on his own.\nBut if the Twin Jewels are involved...
MID_EV14_067_m01_016: I guess we know for certain that Arago is as well.
MID_EV14_067_m01_017: Is it possible that the massacre didn't happen\nbecause of a small, shadowy cohort seeking profit?
MID_EV14_067_m01_018: But rather, a conspiracy on a national scale?
MID_EV14_067_m01_019: That would suggest that the names in the Mahdel\nList were just...the scapegoats.
MID_EV14_067_m01_020: A list of people for us to look at so we were\ndistracted from the darker truth.
MID_EV14_067_m01_021: Leda, if our foe is...an entire nation—or nations,\nI should say—we hardly stand a chance.
MID_EV14_067_m01_022: The bonds between Arago and the Dagdan Empire\nare strong. My lady Kalla's hands would be tied.
MID_EV14_067_m01_023: Well! Now that we have all this evidence, could we\nnot present our findings to the Divine Sovereign?
MID_EV14_067_m01_024: I'd only caution that we have no idea who is involved\nor how far this conspiracy extends.
MID_EV14_067_m01_025: It's possible... It's possible the Divine Sovereign is\ninvolved as well.
MID_EV14_067_m01_026: He did condone the siege of Cydonia, even if\nMahdel's testimony was the catalyst.
MID_EV14_067_m01_027: But if that's the case, then...well, there's nothing we\ncan do, even with Kalla's help.
MID_EV14_067_m01_028: All we know for certain is that something big is\nin motion.
MID_EV14_067_m01_029: We have to tread even more carefully and try to\nlearn all we can.
MID_EV14_067_m01_030: I don't care if it means taking on the empire and all\nits temples... I will kill Bertrand.
MID_EV14_067_m01_031: Finally, he's in my reach.
MID_EV14_042_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_042_m01_001: You've acquitted yourself impressively in the games.
MID_EV14_042_m01_002: And with this victory, you advance to the main\nmatches of the competition.
MID_EV14_042_m01_003: I summoned you to congratulate you on your\nprogress—but also to ask you a question.
MID_EV14_042_m01_004: If you win the Heroic Games, what request will you\nmake of me?
MID_EV14_042_m01_005: Ah...
MID_EV14_042_m01_006: Don't worry too much if it's sensitive. I will not\ndisclose anything we discuss.
MID_EV14_042_m01_007: <NCA>Say your wish.
MID_EV14_042_m01_008: I wish...for the life of the White-Maned Demon.\nOf Bertrand.
MID_EV14_042_m01_009: Ah... Could I ask why?
MID_EV14_042_m01_010: My name is Leilidahna Guillermo Cohendia.
MID_EV14_042_m01_011: My father was Viceroy Guillermo of Cydonia,\nwho was murdered during the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_EV14_042_m01_012: I see. I knew Kalla had given you her support\nin the games...
MID_EV14_042_m01_013: I never imagined that this might be the reason.
MID_EV14_042_m01_014: I chose to enter the Heroic Games to take revenge\nupon my father's murderer.
MID_EV14_042_m01_015: And restore my father's good name after he was\nslandered and undermined.
MID_EV14_042_m01_016: Stark words. You're claiming the official story of the\nsiege was a misrepresentation?
MID_EV14_042_m01_017: Yes. And this will prove it.
MID_EV14_042_m01_018: A list...with names crossed out in blood. And an ingot\nof orichalcum.
MID_EV14_042_m01_019: Explain what these items mean.
MID_EV14_042_m01_020: This list, Father Mahdel wrote. He entrusted it to me\non the day he died.
MID_EV14_042_m01_021: It's a record of the names and actions of those who\nstarted the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_EV14_042_m01_022: And the orichalcum?
MID_EV14_042_m01_023: I recovered it while I was tracking down\nthose culprits.
MID_EV14_042_m01_024: The orichalcum from the mines in Cydonia, now an\nAragonian territory...
MID_EV14_042_m01_025: It's being smuggled into Dagsion every month—\nin huge quantities.
MID_EV14_042_m01_026: *sigh*
MID_EV14_042_m01_027: Answer me this question, Lord Solel.
MID_EV14_042_m01_028: Why did you allow the kingdom of Arago to destroy\nmy home? To invade Cydonia?
MID_EV14_042_m01_029: Mahdel showed me credible evidence that the\nviceroy was a corrupt, oppressive leader.
MID_EV14_042_m01_030: I had no reason to doubt him.
MID_EV14_042_m01_031: You didn't consider he might have been lying?
MID_EV14_042_m01_032: Why would I? Cydonia was not responding to our\nattempts at contact.
MID_EV14_042_m01_033: After a slew of issues—not least the suspicious death\nof a key figure in negotiations.
MID_EV14_042_m01_034: The Aragonians' anger at Cydonia threatened to\ndestroy the kingdom.
MID_EV14_042_m01_035: So you sacrificed the county to appease them?
MID_EV14_042_m01_036: Cydonia was methodically isolated from the empire,\nand tensions were stoked in Arago.
MID_EV14_042_m01_037: It was a plot carried out by those named in this list.
MID_EV14_042_m01_038: I notice a lack of any objective evidence to prove\nyou're telling the truth.
MID_EV14_042_m01_039: Or corroboration of the claims made on this list.
MID_EV14_042_m01_040: If we wanted to investigate, I'd say we could talk to\nthe people whose names are written here, but... Well.
MID_EV14_042_m01_041: Father Mahdel gave his life to atone for his part in\nall this. I believe his claims.
MID_EV14_042_m01_042: Then there is one thing I can offer you.
MID_EV14_042_m01_043: If you win the Heroic Games and prove the heavens\nare on your side...I will believe what you say.
MID_EV14_042_m01_044: This is a method of determining truth that my\nbrother Mars often suggests.
MID_EV14_042_m01_045: <NCA>Agree to it.
MID_EV14_042_m01_046: Alright. Then that's what I'll do.
MID_EV14_042_m01_047: Whew.
MID_EV14_042_m01_048: Anna, could I ask you to listen to my ramblings?
MID_EV14_042_m01_049: There's no one else around, so I think we can\nspeak freely.
MID_EV14_042_m01_050: I fear...I may have been mistaken in my judgment.
MID_EV14_042_m01_051: There may be a need to reexamine the events\nleading up to the Siege of Cydonia.
MID_EV14_042_m01_052: Without Magistra Raksha and the others finding\nout, please.
MID_EV14_042_m01_053: Understood.
MID_EV14_043_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_043_m01_001: I appreciate your efforts. Let me know if you find\nanything else.
MID_EV14_043_m01_002: *sigh*
MID_EV14_043_m01_003: Looking downcast. What's the matter?
MID_EV14_043_m01_004: You're up to something, I can tell.
MID_EV14_043_m01_005: I had one of my soldiers look into the chancellor.
MID_EV14_043_m01_006: Find any interesting information?
MID_EV14_043_m01_007: An interesting...absence of information. Chancellor\nMartila's origins are a complete mystery.
MID_EV14_043_m01_008: Her background's falsified, as far as I can tell.\nAnd going back past a certain point, it's untraceable.
MID_EV14_043_m01_009: Should we really be following this woman's orders?
MID_EV14_043_m01_010: A loyal soldier like you, questioning his leader's\nmotivations?
MID_EV14_043_m01_011: She's adhering to what King Hasdrubal wanted.\nBesides, King Gilchris trusts her.
MID_EV14_043_m01_012: That's what bothers me.
MID_EV14_043_m01_013: It's all so...tidy. The two people who benefited most\nfrom His Majesty's death...
MID_EV14_043_m01_014: Nathan. Listen to me. Don't you ever, ever talk like\nthat to anyone else.
MID_EV14_043_m01_015: Unless you want the same treatment Bertrand got.
MID_EV14_043_m01_016: What's that supposed to mean? Wait—you agree\nwith me. You think it was a conspiracy?
MID_EV14_043_m01_017: Obviously. If anything, I'm surprised you're only\nfiguring it out now.
MID_EV14_043_m01_018: I mean, really. How naïve can you be? I'm starting\nto worry you won't hang in there.
MID_EV14_043_m01_019: At least I know you worry about me.
MID_EV14_043_m01_020: Nathan, have you ever heard the chancellor\nplay her vihuela?
MID_EV14_043_m01_021: When would I have possibly had the chance\nto hear... Wait, what does that matter?
MID_EV14_043_m01_022: I heard it once. It was a heavenly sound.
MID_EV14_043_m01_023: A talent like hers is rare in all of Dagdan history.
MID_EV14_043_m01_024: They say it's why Lord Garland, previous head of\nHouse Amalfrida, fell in love with her.
MID_EV14_043_m01_025: He was so enamored by the music that he took her\ninto his home.
MID_EV14_043_m01_026: Then she became his concubine... Then she became\nchancellor.
MID_EV14_043_m01_027: Now her political opponents are ousted, and the\ncountry's under her thumb.
MID_EV14_043_m01_028: The beauty of her playing... It brought to mind the\nVirtuosa of Heaven and Earth. Heard of her?
MID_EV14_043_m01_029: You know better than anyone that I'm not one for\nthe arts.
MID_EV14_043_m01_030: She was considered to be equal to the bard Cohen—\nable to charm all those who heard her perform.
MID_EV14_043_m01_031: Final wife of Vandahl, the Swashbuckler King.
MID_EV14_043_m01_032: Maria was her name.
MID_EV14_043_m01_033: How do you know so much about her?
MID_EV14_043_m01_034: If you trace my ancestry, I'm descended from House\nVandahl. These stories were passed down to me.
MID_EV14_043_m01_035: King Gilchris is also of Vandahl. Which might be\nwhy I feel a connection with him...
MID_EV14_043_m01_036: Of course, even if it's all true, this would have\nhappened more than five hundred years ago.
MID_EV14_043_m01_037: But...say the legendary musician somehow survived.
MID_EV14_043_m01_038: Changed her name—took over governance of\na kingdom. I don't want to believe it, but...
MID_EV14_043_m01_039: It's possible, if she were a demigod.
MID_EV14_043_m01_040: No, demigods' lifespans usually don't exceed five\nhundred years.
MID_EV14_043_m01_041: Which would make her... Well, it would make\nher a god.
MID_EV14_043_m01_042: So, the gods could be behind all this? But why?
MID_EV14_043_m01_043: I suppose you'd have to ask them.